-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/530673a2-4f93-4c6b-a6c9-d608f6674dcf
-- title:
--   Conditional transversal splitting is controlled by transport energy
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, let $o_1,o_2:\{0,1\}^n\to\{0,1\}$ be fixed Boolean oracle functions, and let $q\in\mathbb Q$. For a paired state $X\subseteq E=[n]\times\{0,1\}$, put $a(X)=q^{d(X)}$, where $d(X)=n\mathbin{\dot-}\operatorname{pairedRank}_{r,o_1,o_2}(X)$ uses the program's rank routine and truncated natural subtraction. Regard these rational weights as real numbers when summing real observables. For a partial assignment $\tau:[n]\to\{\bot,0,1\}$, let $\mathcal T_\tau$ be the transversals selecting the prescribed label at every assigned pair, and write
--
--   $$z_\tau=\sum_{X\in\mathcal T_\tau}a(X),\qquad m_\tau=\frac{\sum_{X\in\mathcal T_\tau}a(X)H(X)}{z_\tau},\qquad M_\tau=\sum_{X\in\mathcal T_\tau}a(X)(H(X)-m_\tau)^2.$$
--
--   Here $H$ is a real function on all paired states. A transversal selects exactly one label at every pair. For a real array $\kappa(X,Y)$ on paired states, define the restricted energy
--
--   $$\mathcal E_\tau(H)=\frac12\sum_{\substack{X,Y\subseteq E\\X,Y\text{ respect }\tau}}\kappa(X,Y)(H(X)-H(Y))^2.$$
--
--   Respecting $\tau$ means containing its prescribed label and excluding its mate at every assigned coordinate; other coordinates are unrestricted.
--
--   Assume $n>0$, $0<q\le1$, and that $o_1,o_2$ are exact independence oracles for matroids $M_1,M_2$ with full ground $[n]$ and common rank $r$. Let $w_{ij}>0$ be rational multipliers for every distinct ordered pair. Assign weight $a(X)$ to a transversal, weight $w_{ij}a(X)$ to a state whose classifier reports empty pair $i$ and full pair $j$, and zero weight to invalid states. Let $Z$ be the sum of these weights and $\pi$ their normalized probability law. Let $Q(X,Y)$ be the proposal probability obtained by drawing two labels independently and uniformly from $E$ and transposing them in $X$, and set $\kappa(X,Y)=Q(X,Y)\min\{\pi(X),\pi(Y)\}$.
--
--   Fix an assignment $\sigma$, a free coordinate $k$, and any real observable $H$. Write $\sigma_b=\sigma[k\mapsto b]$, $s_b=z_{\sigma_b}$, $z=z_\sigma$, and
--
--   $$c^\sigma_{kt}=\sum_{\substack{X\text{ respects }\sigma\\\operatorname{classify}(X)=\operatorname{defect}(k,t)}}a(X),\qquad V=\sum_{\substack{t:\sigma(t)=\bot\\t\ne k}}\frac{c^\sigma_{kt}}{w_{tk}}.$$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$\frac{s_0s_1}{z}(m_{\sigma_0}-m_{\sigma_1})^2\le\left(1+\frac{2V}{z}\right)Z(2n^2)\mathcal E_\sigma(H).$$
--
--   This is the local transport estimate before imposing multiplier-goodness bounds or choosing the split coordinate.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ConditionalTransversalSplitTransport.lean#L117-L445

